### Scope Contract 1.1: Execute VFS Unit Tests
**Objective:** Verify VFS data integrity before any VFS-dependent work proceeds  
**Risk Level:** Low (read-only, verification only)  
**Estimated Duration:** 2-4 hours  
**Dependencies:** None

#### Current State
- 4 test files exist in `tests/unit/vfs/` but execution status unknown
- VFS data integrity is foundation for all catalogue operations
- Zero production impact — pure verification

#### Target State
- All 4 VFS test files execute without errors
- 28/28 tests passing (7 per file × 4 files)
- CI integration prepared for automated execution

#### DoD Sequence

**DoD 1.1.1 — Execute Data Integrity Tests**
- [ ] Run: `npx tsx tests/unit/vfs/data-integrity.test.ts`
- [ ] Verify: Console shows "🎉 All Data Integrity Tests Passed!"
- [ ] Verify: Exit code 0
- [ ] On failure: Document failing assertions, STOP sprint, escalate

**DoD 1.1.2 — Execute Slug Resolution Tests**
- [ ] Run: `npx tsx tests/unit/vfs/slug-resolution.test.ts`
- [ ] Verify: Console shows "🎉 All Slug Resolution Tests Passed!"
- [ ] Verify: All 20 leaf slugs resolve correctly
- [ ] Verify: Exit code 0

**DoD 1.1.3 — Execute Descendant Unrolling Tests**
- [ ] Run: `npx tsx tests/unit/vfs/descendant-unrolling.test.ts`
- [ ] Verify: Console shows "🎉 All Descendant Unrolling Tests Passed!"
- [ ] Verify: Header unroll returns correct subtree
- [ ] Verify: Exit code 0

**DoD 1.1.4 — Execute GROQ Parameter Tests**
- [ ] Run: `npx tsx tests/unit/vfs/groq-parameter.test.ts`
- [ ] Verify: Console shows "🎉 All GROQ Parameter Tests Passed!"
- [ ] Verify: GROQ key parameter formatting correct
- [ ] Verify: Exit code 0

**DoD 1.1.5 — Document Results**
- [ ] Create: `tests/unit/vfs/TEST_RESULTS.md`
- [ ] Record: Timestamp, Node version, pass/fail per file
- [ ] Commit: Difficulty 2 - D, Configuration (VFS): execute unit tests and document results

#### Verification Methods

**Method A — Automated Test Execution:**
```powershell
npx tsx tests/unit/vfs/data-integrity.test.ts
npx tsx tests/unit/vfs/slug-resolution.test.ts
npx tsx tests/unit/vfs/descendant-unrolling.test.ts
npx tsx tests/unit/vfs/groq-parameter.test.ts
```

**Method B — Result Verification:**
```powershell
# Verify all tests passed (PowerShell)
$testFiles = @(
  "tests/unit/vfs/data-integrity.test.ts",
  "tests/unit/vfs/slug-resolution.test.ts",
  "tests/unit/vfs/descendant-unrolling.test.ts",
  "tests/unit/vfs/groq-parameter.test.ts"
)
foreach ($file in $testFiles) {
  npx tsx $file
  if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Write-Host "FAILED: $file"; exit 1 }
}
Write-Host "✅ All 4 VFS test files passed"
```

#### Risk Mitigation

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|------------|--------|------------|
| Test environment not configured | Low | High | Pre-sprint verification SE-3 |
| Tests fail due to data issues | Medium | High | Stop sprint, fix VFS build script first |
| Node version incompatibility | Low | Medium | Use Node 20+ as specified in package.json |

#### Scope Boundaries

**IN SCOPE:**
- Execute existing test files
- Document results
- Prepare CI integration YAML

**OUT OF SCOPE:**
- Fix failing tests (escalate if failures occur)
- Modify VFS build logic
- Production code changes

**FORBIDDEN:**
- Do not modify test files during this scope
- Do not modify `data/catalogue-index.json` directly
- Do not skip tests or ignore failures

