### Scope Contract 2.2: Create 3 Specialized Agents
**Objective:** Build Tier 2 specialized agents for high-error domains  
**Risk Level:** Low (documentation-only, no code changes)  
**Estimated Duration:** 6-8 hours  
**Dependencies:** 2.1 (MCP retrieval must work)

#### Target State
- 3 specialized agent personas in `agents/` directory
- Domain-specific knowledge embedded
- Tools and failure modes documented
- Ready for AI session routing

#### DoD Sequence

**DoD 2.2.1 — Create VFS Specialist Agent**
- [ ] Create: `agents/vfs-specialist.md`
- [ ] Document: Domain scope (Virtual File System)
- [ ] Document: Key knowledge
  - `slugToIdMap` for leaf-level lookups
  - `unrollDescendantKeys()` for subtree queries
  - `slotMetadataMap` structure and constraints
  - O(1) path-based prefix matching
- [ ] Document: Tools available
  - Read: `data/catalogue-index.json`
  - Read: `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`
  - Read-only: `app/actions/categories.ts` (for context)
- [ ] Document: Common patterns with code examples
- [ ] Document: Known failure modes
  | Symptom | Cause | Fix |
  | Empty product list | Invalid keys in GROQ query | Verify keys exist in slotMetadataMap |
  | Wrong category products | Using slug instead of ID | Use slugToIdMap for translation |

**DoD 2.2.2 — Create Sanity Schema Specialist Agent**
- [ ] Create: `agents/sanity-schema-specialist.md`
- [ ] Document: Domain scope (Sanity CMS schema design)
- [ ] Document: Key knowledge
  - Typegen is ABSOLUTE source of truth
  - GROQ must respect generated type contracts
  - Never manually define conflicting types
  - Data flow: Schema → Studio → GROQ → RSC → Props → Client
- [ ] Document: Tools available
  - Read: `sanity/schemaTypes/**`
  - Read: `sanity.types.ts`
  - Run: `sanity typegen generate`
- [ ] Document: Common patterns with code examples
- [ ] Document: Known failure modes
  | Symptom | Cause | Fix |
  | Type errors after schema change | Forgot to regenerate types | Run `sanity typegen generate` |
  | GROQ returns wrong shape | Query doesn't match type contract | Verify query against generated types |

**DoD 2.2.3 — Create UI Component Specialist Agent**
- [ ] Create: `agents/ui-component-specialist.md`
- [ ] Document: Domain scope (Next.js 15 App Router, React Server Components)
- [ ] Document: Key knowledge
  - Primary pages MUST be Server Components
  - Data fetching parallelized on server
  - NO arbitrary "use client" directives
  - Scoped Tailwind classes ONLY
- [ ] Document: Tools available
  - Read/Write: `app/**`
  - Read/Write: `components/**`
  - Read: `SYSTEM_COHERENCE.md` (design system)
- [ ] Document: Common patterns with code examples
- [ ] Document: Styling constraints
  - NEVER modify global CSS files
  - Use scoped Tailwind classes
  - Follow 8pt grid system (py-20, gap-24)
  - Use design system aliases (text-display-2, text-cap)
- [ ] Document: Known failure modes
  | Symptom | Cause | Fix |
  | Hydration mismatch | Server/client render differ | Check "use client" placement |
  | Styles not applying | Global CSS modified | Revert to scoped Tailwind |

**DoD 2.2.4 — Create Agent Orchestration Table**
- [ ] Add to `.windsurfrules` or `architecture.md`:
  ```markdown
  ## Agent Orchestration
  
  | File Pattern | Suggested Agent |
  |--------------|-----------------|
  | `sanity/schemaTypes/**` | sanity-schema-specialist |
  | `app/**/checkout/**` | checkout-fsm-specialist |
  | `data/catalogue*.json` | vfs-specialist |
  | `app/globals.css` | ui-specialist |
  | `tests_e2e/**` | testing-specialist |
  
  ### Manual Routing Commands
  - `/vfs [query]` - Route to VFS specialist
  - `/sanity [query]` - Route to Sanity specialist
  - `/ui [query]` - Route to UI specialist
  ```

**DoD 2.2.5 — Verification**
- [ ] Review: All 3 agent files complete
- [ ] Verify: Agent files follow consistent format
- [ ] Verify: Tools/paths are accurate (exist in codebase)
- [ ] Verify: Failure modes are real issues encountered

